   ],
   "duration": 17.885,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "A follower's own log genuinely diverges from the leader's, at one point.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.426
    },
    {
     "text": "The leader retries, backing up one entry at a time. Does it genuinely find the real common prefix, and overwrite only the divergent suffix?",
     "start": 6.146,
     "end": 17.535
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 121,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "01a": {
   "hash": "5bf369c347f61ab2",
   "takes": [
    "9995c204b819e717847b",
    "913cc3dde1a08ab3830e"
   ],
   "duration": 4.459,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Yes, genuinely.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 1.42
    },
    {
     "text": "It finds the real common prefix.",
     "start": 1.84,
     "end": 4.109
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -4.9,
   "wpm": 108,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "02": {
   "hash": "2884b668b03d1c53",
   "takes": [
    "6f0888e63847f7099ef4"
   ],
   "duration": 10.157,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Run it for real: the repair genuinely finds the common prefix, and overwrites the follower's divergent suffix exactly.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 9.807
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.2,
   "wpm": 106,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03": {
   "hash": "48ad5f8872f214a8",
   "takes": [
    "ae2a5739b6401fff275f",
    "be57e2ace59ade9b5e63"
   ],
   "duration": 13.035,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now a single entry from a previous term already sits on a real majority of the cluster.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.546
    },
    {
     "text": "Does the leader genuinely count it as committed, just from that real majority alone?",
     "start": 7.266,
     "end": 12.685
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -3.1,
   "wpm": 143,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03a": {
   "hash": "984837336818a5e4",
   "takes": [
    "12f9269709fe56730f79",
    "e6dc1ffaea075ced0235"
   ],
   "duration": 4.507,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "No.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 0.624
    },
    {
     "text": "A real majority alone was genuinely not enough.",
     "start": 1.044,
     "end": 4.157
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -15.9,
   "true_peak": -4.3,
   "wpm": 120,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04": {
   "hash": "aa10d00a399d0f71",
   "takes": [
    "42154b76252ee4526a51"
   ],
   "duration": 8.969,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Run it for real: genuinely not committed. A previous term's own real majority alone is genuinely not enough.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 8.619
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.7,
   "wpm": 120,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "05": {
   "hash": "50af3404aba438fb",
   "takes": [
    "76b97bda49b0f565fd7a",
    "0f64a0cbd1c0157228fa"
   ],
   "duration": 15.575,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now the leader also replicates one real entry from its own current term, to the identical majority.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.832
    },
    {
     "text": "Does that entry genuinely commit, and does the earlier entry genuinely commit along with it?",
     "start": 7.552,
     "end": 15.225
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.8,
   "wpm": 123,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "05a": {
   "hash": "a4a0ba1a4dda8a06",
   "takes": [
    "df64a1d2578e646326e7",
    "74d654d5dce0f02856f6"
   ],
   "duration": 4.736,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Both, genuinely.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 1.576
    },
    {
     "text": "One real commitment reaches backward too.",
     "start": 1.996,
     "end": 4.386
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 101,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "06": {
   "hash": "769446c87ca2e4d4",
   "takes": [
    "45e19efe36a293ad29d9"
   ],
   "duration": 8.779,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Run it for real: the current-term entry genuinely commits, and the earlier entry genuinely commits right along with it.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 8.429
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 137,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "07": {
   "hash": "81d362f99101f1fb",
   "takes": [
    "1303d8e128ddaebe8469",
    "04182fb68e787e6768eb"
   ],
   "duration": 13.693,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "One real, foundational paper on this exact subject states this rule directly, in its own words.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 7.452
    },
    {
     "text": "Only entries from the leader's own current term are ever committed by counting replicas.",
     "start": 7.872,
     "end": 13.343
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 131,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "08": {
   "hash": "d6112723a358ca8d",
   "takes": [
    "8a3dd3515983a00ab97a",
    "bf5e1a7c9e49262e18c8"
   ],
   "duration": 15.817,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "A real, widely used consensus implementation in Rust keeps its own log genuinely separate from the application's own state machine.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 8.683
    },
    {
     "text": "That separation is exactly what lets consensus itself be tested against a trivial state machine first.",
     "start": 9.103,
     "end": 15.467
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.0,
   "true_peak": -3.0,
   "wpm": 137,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "09": {
   "hash": "8b5addb5c4226f80",
   "takes": [
    "0718ed5c2a8bd9de9a80"
   ],
   "duration": 12.897,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Run it for real, all together: the repair, the previous-term refusal, and the current-term commitment, measured on one real log and one real follower.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 12.547
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 121,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "10": {
   "hash": "52302e8333aa0bd3",
   "takes": [
    "56e8f4d3f9f639273d90",
    "7ace8e0f95e343eb19e2",
    "2156634297bbaa31153f"
   ],
   "duration": 35.849,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "So here's the real shape of this whole topic: committing is never about a count alone, and repairing is never about guessing where two logs went wrong.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 10.125
    },
    {
     "text": "A log entry only counts once a real majority holds it under the exact term the leader is currently running, which is why an old, already-widespread entry still has to wait.",
     "start": 10.545,
     "end": 22.698
    },
    {
     "text": "And fixing a broken follower never means special-casing anything; the leader just keeps stepping backward until the numbers finally agree, then lets ordinary replication take it from there.",
     "start": 23.118,
     "end": 35.499
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 147,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  }
 }
